From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] spmi: mtk-pmif: set the channel up before adding buses

Since the multi-bus support, mtk_spmi_probe() fills in arb->chan only
after mtk_spmi_bus_probe() has called spmi_controller_add() for every bus.
spmi_controller_add() registers the slave devices, and a slave driver that
is already registered probes them right away, or asynchronously while
mtk_spmi_probe() goes on. Until arb->chan is set, all its register indices
are zero, so a read or write in that window polls PMIF_INIT_DONE instead
of the SWINF status register and writes the command into PMIF_INIT_DONE.

This window is open when the PMIC drivers are built in: drivers/regulator
links before drivers/spmi, so the MT6315 and MT6363 regulator drivers are
already registered when the arbiter probes.

Set the channel up before probing the buses.

Fixes: 078117963b2c ("spmi: mtk-pmif: Add multi-bus support for SPMI 2.0")
---
diff --git a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
index ef3cf4e..c605643 100644
--- a/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
+++ b/drivers/spmi/spmi-mtk-pmif.c
@@ -811,6 +811,17 @@ static int mtk_spmi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, arb);
 
+	/*
+	 * Set the channel up before the buses: adding a bus registers its
+	 * slaves, and their drivers may probe and use the bus right away.
+	 */
+	chan_offset = PMIF_CHAN_OFFSET * arb->data->soc_chan;
+	arb->chan.ch_sta = PMIF_SWINF_0_STA + chan_offset;
+	arb->chan.wdata = PMIF_SWINF_0_WDATA_31_0 + chan_offset;
+	arb->chan.rdata = PMIF_SWINF_0_RDATA_31_0 + chan_offset;
+	arb->chan.ch_send = PMIF_SWINF_0_ACC + chan_offset;
+	arb->chan.ch_rdy = PMIF_SWINF_0_VLD_CLR + chan_offset;
+
 	if (!arb->data->num_spmi_buses) {
 		ret = mtk_spmi_bus_probe(pdev, node, arb->data, &arb->bus[cur_bus]);
 		if (ret)
@@ -828,13 +839,6 @@ static int mtk_spmi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
-	chan_offset = PMIF_CHAN_OFFSET * arb->data->soc_chan;
-	arb->chan.ch_sta = PMIF_SWINF_0_STA + chan_offset;
-	arb->chan.wdata = PMIF_SWINF_0_WDATA_31_0 + chan_offset;
-	arb->chan.rdata = PMIF_SWINF_0_RDATA_31_0 + chan_offset;
-	arb->chan.ch_send = PMIF_SWINF_0_ACC + chan_offset;
-	arb->chan.ch_rdy = PMIF_SWINF_0_VLD_CLR + chan_offset;
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
